# cost_test.tcyr — cost recommendation against the REAL shipped pricing file,
# plus crafted rows parsed in memory and from a temp file.
#
# Added 2.5.5. Through 2.5.4 nothing called load_cloud_instances,
# recommend_instances or cost_to_json, and the loader had the {"instances":
# [...]} wrapper defect load_models lost in 2.3.22: every --cost run saw one
# instance of the file's 18 (the 8x H100 at $98.32/hr). Like
# model_catalog_test, this unit asserts against data/cloud_pricing.json as
# shipped, so loader and data stay gated together. Run from the repo root.

